WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.463 --> 00:00:06.760
(light playful music)

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:07.593
- Hey there.

00:00:07.593 --> 00:00:09.880
I'm Aria and I love making new friends,

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:10.750
and apparently,

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:13.650
one of LinkedIn's slogans
is Relationships Matter.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:16.533
So I figured why not look into
the validity of that claim

00:00:16.533 --> 00:00:18.600
by trying to build a genuine connection

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:19.942
with someone within seven days,

00:00:19.942 --> 00:00:22.398
and hopefully make a new
friend along the way.

00:00:22.398 --> 00:00:24.280
Because that'd be swell.

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:25.420
To gain some insight,

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:28.480
I chat with LinkedIn
expert, Viveka von Rosen.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:29.313
- Like a real friend.

00:00:29.313 --> 00:00:31.160
- [Aria] A real friend.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:34.630
- I do believe you can find a
friend in seven days or less.

00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:35.978
Everything we do on LinkedIn

00:00:35.978 --> 00:00:38.619
is so that we could have those age-to-age,

00:00:38.619 --> 00:00:41.280
those human-to-human relationships.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:44.283
- [Aria] To start, Viveka
helps me remodel my profile.

00:00:44.283 --> 00:00:47.129
- We want it so that after
reading your profile,

00:00:47.129 --> 00:00:49.520
that they almost feel like they know you.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:52.970
Photos, video, you have the
opportunity to upload media.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:54.150
- [Aria] Taking Viveka's advice,

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:56.740
I take a set of new photos for my page.

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:58.930
- You wanna create your LinkedIn profile

00:00:58.930 --> 00:01:00.810
and you wanna create your
engagement on LinkedIn,

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:03.480
and you wanna create
your content on LinkedIn

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:05.860
to reflect your very, very best self.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:08.130
The best part of who you are.

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:10.400
And then the other thing
is recommendations.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:11.750
- [Aria] Seeking recommendations,

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:14.450
I reach out to people I feel know me best.

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:17.763
- [Aria] And finally,

00:01:17.763 --> 00:01:20.240
to add extra certifications to my profile,

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:22.180
I hire someone off of Craigslist

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:24.530
to teach me a course I developed myself.

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:26.762
When the slideshow
rolls, just roll with it.

00:01:26.762 --> 00:01:30.100
- Oh, now I'll explain
a little bit about...

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:32.050
Should I say that or should
I roll with something else?

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:33.620
- [Viveka] Certainly,
if you've gone to school

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:34.940
or you've gotten certifications

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:36.600
that are necessary in your industry.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:38.360
By all means, add them.

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:41.273
♪ You've got a friend in me ♪

00:01:41.273 --> 00:01:45.440
♪ Yeah, you've got a friend in me ♪

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:49.550
- Okay, so it's been a few days.

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:50.720
I've rebuilt my profile.

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:51.970
My network has grown a bit,

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:53.630
so I think we're ready to get started.

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:54.850
So I'm gonna reach out to a few people

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:55.960
that seem interesting to me,

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:57.590
and I'm gonna give myself five days

00:01:57.590 --> 00:01:59.610
to build some sort of
a friendship with them

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:01.780
before asking them to hang
out with me on the fifth day.

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:03.630
And we'll see what happens.

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:05.770
I start sending out requests to people

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:08.940
with mutual connections who
share similar interests with me.

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:10.014
This guy works in sushi.

00:02:10.014 --> 00:02:11.512
I love sushi.

00:02:11.512 --> 00:02:12.660
Fantastic.

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:13.860
I receive a steady stream

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.593
of accepted requests throughout the day,

00:02:15.593 --> 00:02:19.330
although many of them don't
respond to my first message.

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:22.670
However, I do receive replies
from Kenny, a retired athlete.

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:26.300
And Nico, a former co-worker
of a mutual friend.

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:27.930
Tuesday brings more of the same

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:30.798
with accepted requests
that leave me on read.

00:02:30.798 --> 00:02:31.872
We have a food truck in here today,

00:02:31.872 --> 00:02:33.110
but all I could think about

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:36.150
is why haven't these
people responded to me.

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:38.851
On the plus side, Kenny
and Nico continue to reply

00:02:38.851 --> 00:02:41.660
and I also receive a response from James,

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:45.330
an actor who, like me, went
to high school in Thailand.

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:47.930
So far, Kenny is definitely
top of the class.

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:49.510
He always responds to me.

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:51.540
The poor guy probably thinks I'm crazy.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:52.760
I keep asking him questions.

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:53.593
He keeps responding.

00:02:53.593 --> 00:02:55.380
He never asks me a question.

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:57.050
Hopefully, eventually,
he'll ask me a question.

00:02:57.050 --> 00:02:58.920
I think it will be a victory

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:01.350
when Kenny finally asks me a question.

00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:05.780
But then, on Wednesday, tragedy strikes.

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:07.646
Kenny has left me on read.

00:03:07.646 --> 00:03:09.200
It's not a good thing.

00:03:10.829 --> 00:03:12.890
This is the first time that
Kenny has left me on read.

00:03:17.314 --> 00:03:18.580
- I have gone crazy.

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:21.414
However, soon after,
another twist develops.

00:03:21.414 --> 00:03:24.210
Nico has actually asked me to hang out.

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:26.632
Nico wrote back to me,
he wants to hang out.

00:03:26.632 --> 00:03:27.465
- What did he say?

00:03:27.465 --> 00:03:29.756
- He said, you know, we
should grab a drink and chat.

00:03:29.756 --> 00:03:30.860
Yeah.

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:31.693
- Wow.
- Yeah!

00:03:31.693 --> 00:03:32.526
- Look at you
- I know, I know.

00:03:32.526 --> 00:03:33.359
- You should be like,

00:03:33.359 --> 00:03:34.690
yeah I'm totally down, when are you free?

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:35.960
Okay, I'm walking home right now.

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:38.080
I'm hoping that when I get home,

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:39.130
I'm gonna open up my LinkedIn

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:40.947
and I'll have a message
waiting for me from Nico.

00:03:40.947 --> 00:03:42.542
I won't lie, I'm a little nervous.

00:03:42.542 --> 00:03:45.890
("You're My Best Friend" by Queen)

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:47.550
Nico didn't respond.

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:50.480
Nico is online right now,
and he hasn't responded.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:52.630
Kenny chose to ignore me,

00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:54.730
so I will not go crawling back to Kenny.

00:03:56.415 --> 00:03:57.410
- Screw Kenny?

00:03:57.410 --> 00:03:58.244
Yeah, I agree.

00:03:58.244 --> 00:03:59.890
The one response is from James though.

00:03:59.890 --> 00:04:02.640
And so, maybe James is the one.

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:05.010
But on the penultimate
day of my challenge,

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:07.650
things take a further turn for the worst.

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:09.210
This is the first time
I've opened up LinkedIn

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:12.160
since I started this without
getting a single notification.

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:14.423
Not good.

00:04:14.423 --> 00:04:15.890
- I would go with Nico.

00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:16.723
- Nico's the second one?

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:17.810
- Nico's the one that
asked me to hang out,

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:19.232
but he hasn't responded
since I asked him when.

00:04:19.232 --> 00:04:21.085
- He probably just got busy.
- Yeah.

00:04:21.085 --> 00:04:23.070
James, you have a
personal connection with.

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:24.090
- James is cool.

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:25.040
- Forget the first one. Kenny?

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:26.010
- Kenny? Forget Kenny?

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:27.355
- Yeah. He ghosted you.
- Yeah, and was selfish.

00:04:27.355 --> 00:04:28.188
- Yeah.

00:04:28.188 --> 00:04:29.021
- Kenny, shame on you.

00:04:29.021 --> 00:04:34.021
- But later that day, James
replies to me once again.

00:04:34.070 --> 00:04:35.460
So going into my final day,

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:38.135
I decide that with our
unique Thailand connection,

00:04:38.135 --> 00:04:40.800
I'll see if James wants to hang out.

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:41.633
It's my last day.

00:04:41.633 --> 00:04:43.410
And so today, I'm gonna ask
James to hang out with me.

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:45.500
- Aw, that would be fun.

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:47.240
- Yet, how do you think I
should write the message though?

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:48.073
What should I write?

00:04:48.073 --> 00:04:49.500
- I think you should just be yourself.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:51.794
- So I send James a message
asking him to hang out,

00:04:51.794 --> 00:04:55.120
and then, it becomes a waiting game.

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:56.957
It's 11:26 a.m.

00:04:56.957 --> 00:04:59.360
(Aria sighs)

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:00.620
No response.

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:06.390
- The time is 3:53 p.m.

00:05:08.684 --> 00:05:10.840
No response.

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:11.940
- What did you ask him?

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:12.840
- We should hang out sometime.

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:14.140
Are you free this weekend?

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:16.483
Is that not good?

00:05:16.483 --> 00:05:19.297
- It's very forward, Aria.

00:05:19.297 --> 00:05:21.567
- I think he's gonna leave you at read.

00:05:21.567 --> 00:05:23.606
- I think this is gonna end with you

00:05:23.606 --> 00:05:26.380
making a picnic basket
and getting stood up

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:28.040
and eating the whole baguette yourself

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:29.560
on the end of Echo Park Lake.

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:30.393
- [Aria] I don't know.

00:05:30.393 --> 00:05:32.820
- Hey, you're a great guy.

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:35.408
You don't need more friends.

00:05:35.408 --> 00:05:37.585
- As I arrive home defeated,

00:05:37.585 --> 00:05:42.480
I open up my LinkedIn
to one unread message.

00:05:45.052 --> 00:05:46.719
- Here goes nothing.

00:05:49.150 --> 00:05:50.629
- Okay, so what did we learn?

00:05:50.629 --> 00:05:52.790
Can you use LinkedIn to find a friend?

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:56.220
Honestly, I don't think so.

00:05:57.610 --> 00:05:58.560
For the most part.

00:06:00.510 --> 00:06:01.343
- What's up?

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:04.343
- It's James.

00:06:04.343 --> 00:06:05.176
- It's James.

00:06:05.176 --> 00:06:07.020
- What made you decide just to hang out

00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:10.060
with a guy you met on
LinkedIn less than a week ago?

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:12.560
- It was definitely mainly
the Thailand similarity.

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:13.620
I grew up in Thailand

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:16.134
and he also has some
time spent in Thailand,

00:06:16.134 --> 00:06:20.320
and so I feel like that was
already a unique connection.

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:23.160
And you also didn't seem like a catfisher.

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:24.320
- Regardless of LinkedIn or not,

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:25.153
I think what I learned

00:06:25.153 --> 00:06:26.779
is that you can't really
force a friendship.

00:06:26.779 --> 00:06:28.127
It has to come about organically.

00:06:28.127 --> 00:06:29.750
- And then, they go see you?

00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:30.583
- Yeah!

00:06:30.583 --> 00:06:31.416
- Damn.

00:06:31.416 --> 00:06:33.162
- We just lucked out that James
and I had a lot in common.

00:06:33.162 --> 00:06:35.641
And we got even luckier
that when we met in person,

00:06:35.641 --> 00:06:37.476
he was just as cool.

00:06:37.476 --> 00:06:38.750
I mean, for all we know,

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:42.020
he could've turned out to be deraged.

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:42.853
You never know.

00:06:43.923 --> 00:06:45.186
You never know.

00:06:45.186 --> 00:06:48.186
(light cello music)

00:06:58.100 --> 00:06:59.631
- Oh my God, this is gonna take forever.

00:06:59.631 --> 00:07:00.889
(logo whooshing)

00:07:00.889 --> 00:07:02.500
(logo squeaking)

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:04.470
- Kenny, fuck off and die.

